From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ned <github@edoardo.fyi>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:09:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 087/102] runtime: complete reverse VIF1 GS downloads

Mirror PCSX2 dmaVIF1: DIR=0 downloads use normal transfer mode even when MOD remains chain. Preserve TADR, consume the GS FIFO through the data-side owner, advance MADR/QWC and raise DMAC1 after the copy.

FIFA Street starts CHCR=0x184 in sub_003BF238. The old source-chain walk consumes later readback tags instead, leaving record+8 (observed 0x0102E120) unset while sub_0029DD38 spins. The guest completion store is 0x3BF3E0.

Regression failed before the fix on copied pixels, MADR and CHCR. It now covers incremental downloads, TADR preservation and one VIF1 IRQ per transfer. Correct source-DMA DIR bits in the existing fixtures. Verified ./rx build and ./rx test --full (57/57).

